---
import SectionTitle from "../layouts/SectionTitle.astro";
import PortfolioNav from "../layouts/PortfolioNav.astro";
import VideoScript from "../layouts/VideoScript.astro";
import Video from "../layouts/Video.astro";
import Image from "../layouts/Image.astro";
import Footer from "../layouts/Footer.astro"

---

<html lang="en">
    <body class="gamefeel bg-[#e7e1d8] min-h-screen text-[#292522]">
        <PortfolioNav />
        <SectionTitle
            title="TPS Gamefeel"
            imgsrc="/portfolio/gamefeel.png"
            titlecolor="text-[#e85d32]"
        />
        <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 space-y-3 mb-6">
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p>
                I have developed a third-person shooter system that draws its
                inspiration mainly from Fortnite, due to its accessibility and
                visual feedback (hit markers, bullet trajectories and impact
                effects). It also incorporates several elements from
                Counter-Strike: Global Offensive, notably bullet spread, which
                increases significantly during long bursts of fire or while the
                playable character is moving.
            </p><p>
                The main aim of this system was to create a satisfying shooting
                experience, allowing us to work on the different layers of
                gamefeel to provide the player with additional information.
            </p>
            <h2>Used tools</h2>
            <p>I used Unreal Engine 5.6 in blueprint to create the mechanics.</p>

            <h2>How It Works</h2>
            <p>The basic system allows you to:</p>
            <ul class="list">
                <li>Fire a weapon</li>
                <li>Change weapons by hovering over one</li>
                <li>Replenish your ammunition supply by hovering over a box</li>
                <li>
                    See the damage inflicted on enemies (white for the body and
                    orange for the head)
                </li>
                <li>
                    See the number of rounds remaining in the magazine and those
                    in reserve
                </li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Gamefeel Layers</h2>
            <p>
                Players can enable and disable the gamefeel options from a
                specific menu.
            </p>
            <Image imgsrc="/portfolio/menu.png"/>

            <h3>Gun Sound</h3>
            <p>
                Gives an audio indication of when a shot was fired or while the
                weapon is being reloaded.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/gunsound.mp4" />

            <h3>Bullet Trace</h3>
            <p>
                Shows the visual trajectory of the shot at the moment it was
                fired.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/bullettrace.mp4" />

            <h3>Muzzle Flash</h3>
            <p>Reinforces the impression that a shot was fired</p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/muzzleflash.mp4" />

            <h3>Bloom</h3>
            <p>
                Adds a sense of realism. The dispersion is visually represented
                by the deviation of the crosshair but also by randomly
                generated trajectories that correspond to this deviation.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/bloom.mp4" />
            <h3>Recoil</h3>
            <p>
                Adds another sense of realism. The recoil is randomly calculated
                by adding values to horizontal and vertical look action.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/recul.mp4" />
            <h3>Impacts</h3>
            <p>Adds visual feedback for the hits from the shots fired.</p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/impact.mp4" />

            <h3>Impact Particles</h3>
            <p>
                Complements the previous option by adding particles representing
                the impacts of the shots relative to the surface struck.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/particles.mp4" />

            <h3>Bullet Casings</h3>
            <p>
                Adds visual feedback when a shot is fired. Add an additional
                sound when the casing hit the ground, if the gun sound parameter
                is activated.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/douilles.mp4" />

            <h3>Reduce Damage Based On Distance</h3>
            <p>
                Adds a new layer of realism where weapons have less impact the
                further away the target is.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/damage.mp4" />
            <h3>Visual Hit Markers</h3>
            <p>
                Add a visual feedback showing where the player's eyes are fixed,
                which varies depending on the status of the hit.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/visualhit.mp4" />

            <h3>Audio Hit Markers</h3>
            <p>
                Add an audio feedback to provide a distinctive sound cue so that
                the player can better understand the consequences of hits.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/audiohit.mp4" />

            <h3>Dead Animation</h3>
            <p>
                Add another visual cue so that the player can easily tell
                when an enemy has been defeated and so that this defeat feels
                more natural.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/anim.mp4" />

            <h2>Links</h2>

            <p>
                <span class="bold">Project repository</span>: <a
                    href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/171lwBSpPi2a9iR7YRjEV6ypFhiCRENLy/view?usp=sharing"
                    >https://drive.google.com/file/d/171lwBSpPi2a9iR7YRjEV6ypFhiCRENLy/view?usp=sharing</a
                >
            </p>
            <h2>Inspirations</h2>
            <p>Capcom. (2005). Resident Evil 4 [Video Game]. Capcom. Valve</p>
            <p>
                Corporation & Hidden Path Entertainment. (2012). Counter-Strike:
                Global Offensive [Video Game]. Valve Corporation
            </p>
            <h2>Credits & Resources</h2>
            <h3>Resources Used</h3>
